  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Florida federal contract activity through FY2027 to date shows a sharp drop in obligations compared with prior full fiscal years. Total obligations in Florida are $767M across 4,157 awards with an average award size of $184K. Obligations fell 97.8% year over year. FY22 through FY26 show multibillion-dollar annual totals, with FY22 at $27.3B, FY23 at $31.2B, FY24 at $33.1B, FY25 at $34.1B, and FY26 at $34.7B. FY2027 to date totals are partial and reflect the fiscal year to date position. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buyer in FY2027 to date with $224M, followed by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $148M and the General Services Administration with $140M. BLUE ORIGIN, LLC is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date with $99.2M, followed by AKIMA INFRASTRUCTURE PROTECTION LLC with $69.6M and VETERANS DEVELOPMENT CORPORATION, INC. with $63.1M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the top industry by obligations in FY2027 to date with $103M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What explains the year-over-year change in obligations?",
        "body": "Florida federal contract obligations fell 97.8% year over year. Total obligations in FY2027 to date are $767M, a large decline versus FY26 obligations of $34.7B. The FY2027 total is a fiscal year to date figure and the prior years show much larger full-year totals: FY22 $27.3B, FY23 $31.2B, FY24 $33.1B, FY25 $34.1B, FY26 $34.7B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries are driving FY2027 to date spending?",
        "body": "Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buying agency in FY2027 to date with $224M. National Aeronautics and Space Administration and General Services Administration follow with $148M and $140M respectively. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry by obligations with $103M, and Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation is next with $99.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
